WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.240
Good Clinical Practice (GCP) is an&nbsp;
international ethical and scientific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.960
quality standard for designing, conducting,&nbsp;
recording and reporting clinical trials that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.960
involve the participation of human subjects.&nbsp;
Regardless of whether a clinical trial is a large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.240
multi-center study in patients or a small clinical&nbsp;
pharmacological study in healthy subjects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.040
the relevant GCP standard should be followed by&nbsp;
the sponsoring company of the healthcare product,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.360
the investigators, the ethics committees&nbsp;
and any clinical research organizations.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.081
Companies undertaking a clinical trial must&nbsp;
follow certain procedures and practices&nbsp;

00:00:41.081 --> 00:00:43.840
Companies undertaking a clinical trial should&nbsp;
develop written procedures for implementing GCP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.720
Such procedures may include, but&nbsp;
are not limited to, the following:

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.680
• Investigator site selection
• Regulatory document collection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.720
review and submission
• Financial disclosure&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.120
• Investigator site initiation
• Investigational product&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.360
distribution and tracking
• Clinical monitoring of investigator site&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.440
• Investigator site close-out
• Safety reporting&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.280
• Quality assurance audits
• Required documents for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.560
study master file and document retention
• Vendor qualification and oversight (for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:25.840
example, contract research organization)
• Indemnity, compensation and insurance

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.120
Good Clinical Practice and the&nbsp;
International Conference on Harmonization&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:32.720
Prior to the GCP guidance document developed by&nbsp;
the International Conference on Harmonization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.680
(ICH), different jurisdictions had different&nbsp;
guidelines relating to the conduct of clinical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:44.320
trials. With the introduction of ICH GCP,&nbsp;
the conduct of clinical trials globally has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:50.880
become more uniform and practicable. Today, the&nbsp;
implementation of ICH good clinical practice in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.760
most jurisdictions is reasonably similar and the&nbsp;
vast majority of the regulations are the same.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.720
Despite the effort of ICH, there&nbsp;
still exists some local differences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:07.200
For example, the US no longer adheres to&nbsp;
the Declaration of Helsinki in its entirety,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.960
because the declaration considers&nbsp;
placebo-controlled trials unethical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:17.120
in cases where an active drug is available. New&nbsp;
privacy regulations in the EU and the financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.840
disclosure requirements in the US are also making&nbsp;
the clinical trial landscape more complicated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.400
Healthcare product developers should therefore&nbsp;
work to ICH in the context of local regulations.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.760
GCP principles for clinical trials
The regulations, guidance and industry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.400
standards that make up Good Clinical Practice are&nbsp;
intended to provide assurance that the rights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.800
safety and well-being of clinical trial subjects&nbsp;
are protected. GCP is also intended to assure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:51.040
that the research yields quality scientific data.&nbsp;
Fundamentally, Good Clinical Practice requires:

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.760
• Oversight of the local ethics committee(s)
• Verification of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.960
investigator’s qualifications
• A study protocol, investigator’s brochure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.760
informed consent, and the documentation that&nbsp;
is essential for undertaking a clinical trial&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.280
• Monitoring of the clinical trial
• Submission of reports and maintenance of records&nbsp;

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:18.080
• The ICH GCP lays out the responsibilities of&nbsp;
the ethics committees, sponsors and investigators.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.880
The core principles of ICH Good&nbsp;
Clinical Practice are presented below.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.320
Thirteen core principles of GCP
1. Ethical principles: Clinical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.920
trials should be conducted in accordance&nbsp;
with the ethical principles that have their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.560
origin in the Declaration of Helsinki,&nbsp;
and that are consistent with GCP and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.040
the applicable regulatory requirement(s).
2. Favourable benefit(s) vs. risk(s): Before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.040
a trial is initiated, foreseeable&nbsp;
risks and inconveniences should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:49.520
weighed against the anticipated benefit for&nbsp;
the individual trial subject and society.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.600
A trial should be initiated and continued only&nbsp;
if the anticipated benefits justify the risks.&nbsp;

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:02.320
3. Subject’s rights: The rights, safety,&nbsp;
and well-being of the trial subjects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:07.280
are the most important considerations and should&nbsp;
prevail over interests of science and society.&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.240
4. Adequate supporting data: The available&nbsp;
nonclinical and clinical information on an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.400
investigational product should be adequate&nbsp;
to support the proposed clinical trial.&nbsp;

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.880
5. Scientifically sound protocol: Clinical&nbsp;
trials should be scientifically sound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:27.440
and described in a clear, detailed protocol.
6. Independent ethics committee oversight: A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.240
trial should be conducted in compliance with the&nbsp;
protocol that has received prior institutional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.488
review board (IRB)/independent ethics&nbsp;
committee (IEC) approval/favourable opinion.&nbsp;

00:04:35.488 --> 00:04:39.200
7. Medical care by qualified investigator: The&nbsp;
medical care given to, and medical decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.680
made on behalf of, subjects should always be&nbsp;
the responsibility of a qualified physician or,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.720
when appropriate, of a qualified dentist.
8. Qualified personnel: Each individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:54.080
involved in conducting a trial should be qualified&nbsp;
by education, training, and experience to perform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.480
his or her respective task(s).
9. Informed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:02.960
consent: Freely given informed consent&nbsp;
should be obtained from every subject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:08.720
prior to clinical trial participation.
10. Record-keeping: All clinical trial information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.040
should be recorded, handled, and stored in&nbsp;
a way that allows its accurate reporting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.240
interpretation and verification.
11. Subject confidentiality:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:22.080
The confidentiality of records that could identify&nbsp;
subjects should be protected, respecting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.960
privacy and confidentiality rules in accordance&nbsp;
with the applicable regulatory requirement(s).&nbsp;

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.480
12. GMP manufacturing of the investigational&nbsp;
product: Investigational products should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.080
manufactured, handled, and stored&nbsp;
in accordance with applicable good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:41.920
manufacturing practice (GMP). They should be&nbsp;
used in accordance with the approved protocol.&nbsp;

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.640
13. Quality assurance &amp; monitoring:&nbsp;
Systems with procedures that assure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.840
the quality of every aspect of&nbsp;
the trial should be implemented.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.480
Summary
In summary, GCP helps protect the rights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:05.840
safety and well-being of clinical trial&nbsp;
subjects, and assures quality scientific data.

